[^\\\"]*)\\\" confirming the dialogue$/\\n531:      * @throws ElementNotFoundException Thrown by behat_base::find\\n532:      * @param string $element Element we look for\\n533:      * @param string $selectortype The type of what we look for\\n534:      */\\n535:     public function i_click_on_confirming_the_dialogue($element, $selectortype) {\\n536:         $this->i_click_on($element, $selectortype);\\n537:         $this->execute([self::class, 'accept_currently_displayed_alert_dialog'], []);\\n538:         $this->wait_until_the_page_is_ready();\\n539:     }\\n540: \\n541:     /**\\n542:      * Clicks the specified element and dismissing the expected dialogue.\\n543:      *\\n544:      * @When /^I click on \\\"(?P<element_string>(?:[^\\\"]|\\\\\\\\\\\")*)\\\" \\\"(?P<selector_string>[^\\\"]*)\\\" dismissing the dialogue$/\\n545:      * @throws ElementNotFoundException Thrown by behat_base::find\\n546:      * @param string $element Element we look for\\n547:      * @param string $selectortype The type of what we look for\\n548:      */\\n549:     public function i_click_on_dismissing_the_dialogue($element, $selectortype) {\\n550:         $this->i_click_on($element, $selectortype);\\n551:         $this->execute([self::class, 'dismiss_currently_displayed_alert_dialog'], []);\\n552:         $this->wait_until_the_page_is_ready();\\n553:     }\\n554: \\n555:     /**\\n556:      * Click on the element of the specified type which is located inside the second element.\\n557:      *\\n558:      * @When /^I click on \\\"(?P<element_string>(?:[^\\\"]|\\\\\\\\\\\")*)\\\" \\\"(?P<selector_string>[^\\\"]*)\\\" in the \\\"(?P<element_container_string>(?:[^\\\"]|\\\\\\\\\\\")*)\\\" \\\"(?P<text_selector_string>[^\\\"]*)\\\"$/\\n559:      * @param string $element Element we look for\\n560:      * @param string $selectortype The type of what we look for\\n561:      * @param string $nodeelement Element we look in\\n562:      * @param string $nodeselectortype The type of selector where we look in\\n563:      */\\n564:     public function i_click_on_in_the($element, $selectortype, $nodeelement, $nodeselectortype) {\\n565:         $node = $this->get_node_in_container($selectortype, $element, $nodeselectortype, $nodeelement);\\n566:         $node->click();\\n567:     }\\n568: \\n569:     /**\\n570:      * Click on the element with some modifier key pressed (alt, shift, meta or control).\\n571:      *\\n572:      * It is important to note that not all HTML elements are compatible with this step because\\n573:      * the webdriver limitations. For example, alt click on checkboxes with a visible label will\\n574:      * produce a normal checkbox click without the modifier.\\n575:      *\\n576:      * @When I :modifier click on :element :selectortype in the :nodeelement :nodeselectortype\\n577:      * @param string $modifier the extra modifier to press (for example, alt+shift or shift)\\n578:      * @param string $element Element we look for\\n579:      * @param string $selectortype The type of what we look for\\n580:      * @param string $nodeelement Element we look in\\n581:      * @param string $nodeselectortype The type of selector where we look in\\n582:      */\\n583:     public function i_key_click_on_in_the($modifier, $element, $selectortype, $nodeelement, $nodeselectortype) {\\n584:         behat_base::require_javascript_in_session($this->getSession());\\n585: \\n586:         $key = null;\\n587:         switch (strtoupper(trim($modifier))) {\\n588:             case '':\\n589:                 break;\\n590:             case 'SHIFT':\\n591:                 $key = behat_keys::SHIFT;\\n592:                 break;\\n593:             case 'CTRL':\\n594:                 $key = behat_keys::CONTROL;\\n595:                 break;\\n596:             case 'ALT':\\n597:                 $key = behat_keys::ALT;\\n598:                 break;\\n599:             case 'META':\"}"}],"provider":"mcp-json","providerName":"MCP Config"},"isError":false,"timestamp":17948